:TESTCASE-BEGIN:1
:DESC: Test case to test RTM Static Route Add/Delete with IPv4

:PRINT: Topology to be loaded in testapp.c : cross_link_topology();

:PRINT:                                                  +--------+-+
:PRINT:                   +---------+                    | R2       |
:PRINT:               eth1| R1      |eth2     20.1.1.2/24|122.1.1.2 |eth8      
:PRINT:       +-----------+122.1.1.1+--------------------+          +------------------+
:PRINT:       |10.1.1.2/24|         |20.1.1.1/24     eth3|          |50.1.1.1/24       |
:PRINT:       |           +---------+                    +-----+--+-+                  +
:PRINT:       +                                         eth4/  |eth7                   |
:PRINT:       |10.1.1.1/24                      30.1.1.1/24/   |40.1.1.2/24            |
:PRINT:       |eth0                                       /    |                  eth9 |50.1.1.2/24
:PRINT:   +---+---+--+                                   /     |                  +----+-----+
:PRINT:   |          |                                  /      |                  |    R3    |
:PRINT:   | R0       |                                 /       |                  | 122.1.1.3|
:PRINT:   |122.1.1.0 |                                /        |                  |          |
:PRINT:   |          |                               /         |                  +----+-----+
:PRINT:   +---+---+--|               ---------------/          |                       |eth10
:PRINT:       |eth14                /                          |                       |60.1.1.1/24
:PRINT:       |80.1.1.1/24         /                           |                       |
:PRINT:       |                   /                            |                       |
:PRINT:       |                  /                        eth6 |40.1.1.1/24            |
:PRINT:       |             eth5/30.1.1.2/24             +-----+----+                  |
:PRINT:       |           +----/----+                    |   R4     |                  |
:PRINT:       |      eth15|   R5    |eth12    70.1.1.2/24|122.1.1.4 |eth11             |
:PRINT:       +-----------+122.1.1.5|+-------------------+          +------------------+
:PRINT:        80.1.1.2/24|         |70.1.1.1/24    eth13|          |60.1.1.2/24
:PRINT:                  -+---------+                    +----------+

:PRINT: Testing Static Route Installation and Deletion

Add static route to R0 with single nexthop
:STEP:1
:CMD: config node R0 rtm-route prefix 192.168.1.0/24 0 0 0 2 10 gateway 10.1.1.2 interface eth0


Verify the route is installed with all properties
:STEP:2
:CMD: show node R0 ip vrf 0 route 0
:STEP:3
:PATTERN-MATCH:192.168.1.0/24
:STEP:4
:PATTERN-MATCH:Static
:STEP:5
:PATTERN-MATCH:10.1.1.2
:STEP:6
:PATTERN-MATCH:eth0
:STEP:7
:GREP:192.168.1.0/24
:STEP:8
:PATTERN-MATCH:10

Add another static route with different metric
:STEP:9
:CMD: config node R0 rtm-route prefix 172.16.0.0/16 0 0 0 2 20 gateway 10.1.1.2 interface eth0


Verify both routes exist with correct properties
:STEP:10
:CMD: show node R0 ip vrf 0 route 0
:STEP:11
:PATTERN-MATCH:172.16.0.0/16
:STEP:12
:GREP:172.16.0.0/16
:STEP:13
:PATTERN-MATCH:20
:STEP:14
:CMD: show node R0 ip vrf 0 route 0
:STEP:15
:PATTERN-MATCH:192.168.1.0/24

Delete first static route
:STEP:16
:CMD: config node R0 no rtm-route prefix 192.168.1.0/24 0 0 0 2 10 gateway 10.1.1.2 interface eth0


Verify first route is deleted but second remains
:STEP:17
:CMD: show node R0 ip vrf 0 route 0
:STEP:18
:PATTERN-NOT-MATCH:192.168.1.0/24
:STEP:19
:PATTERN-MATCH:172.16.0.0/16

Delete second route
:STEP:20
:CMD: config node R0 no rtm-route prefix 172.16.0.0/16 0 0 0 2 20 gateway 10.1.1.2 interface eth0


Verify both routes are deleted
:STEP:21
:CMD: show node R0 ip vrf 0 route 0
:STEP:22
:PATTERN-NOT-MATCH:192.168.1.0/24
:STEP:23
:PATTERN-NOT-MATCH:172.16.0.0/16

:TESTCASE-END:1


:TESTCASE-BEGIN:2
:DESC: Test case to test RTM ECMP Routes with Multiple Nexthops

:PRINT: Testing ECMP (Equal Cost Multi-Path) Routes

Add first nexthop for ECMP route on R1
:STEP:1
:CMD: config node R1 rtm-route prefix 10.10.10.0/24 0 0 0 2 100 gateway 10.1.1.1 interface eth1


Add second nexthop for same route (ECMP)
:STEP:2
:CMD: config node R1 rtm-route prefix 10.10.10.0/24 0 0 0 2 100 gateway 20.1.1.2 interface eth2


Verify ECMP route with both nexthops
:STEP:3
:CMD: show node R1 ip vrf 0 route 0
:STEP:4
:PATTERN-MATCH:10.10.10.0/24
:STEP:5
:PATTERN-MATCH:Static
:STEP:6
:PATTERN-MATCH:10.1.1.1
:STEP:7
:PATTERN-MATCH:eth1
:STEP:8
:CMD: show node R1 ip vrf 0 route 0
:STEP:9
:PATTERN-MATCH:20.1.1.2
:STEP:10
:PATTERN-MATCH:eth2

Add third nexthop (3-way ECMP)
:STEP:11
:CMD: config node R1 rtm-route prefix 10.10.10.0/24 0 0 0 2 100 gateway 122.1.1.2 interface eth2


Verify 3-way ECMP with all three gateways
:STEP:12
:CMD: show node R1 ip vrf 0 route 0
:STEP:13
:PATTERN-MATCH:10.10.10.0/24
:STEP:14
:PATTERN-MATCH:122.1.1.2

Delete one nexthop
:STEP:15
:CMD: config node R1 no rtm-route prefix 10.10.10.0/24 0 0 0 2 100 gateway 10.1.1.1 interface eth1


Verify 2-way ECMP remains with correct gateways
:STEP:16
:CMD: show node R1 ip vrf 0 route 0
:STEP:17
:PATTERN-MATCH:10.10.10.0/24
:STEP:18
:PATTERN-MATCH:20.1.1.2
:STEP:19
:PATTERN-MATCH:122.1.1.2

Delete remaining nexthops
:STEP:20
:CMD: config node R1 no rtm-route prefix 10.10.10.0/24 0 0 0 2 100 gateway 20.1.1.2 interface eth2
:STEP:21
:CMD: config node R1 no rtm-route prefix 10.10.10.0/24 0 0 0 2 100 gateway 122.1.1.2 interface eth2


Verify route is completely deleted
:STEP:22
:CMD: show node R1 ip vrf 0 route 0
:STEP:23
:PATTERN-NOT-MATCH:10.10.10.0/24

:TESTCASE-END:2


:TESTCASE-BEGIN:3
:DESC: Test case to test RTM ISIS Routes with Different Sub-Protocols

:PRINT: Testing ISIS Route Types (L1 Internal, L2 Internal, L1 External, L2 External)

Add L1 ISIS Internal route on R2
:STEP:1
:CMD: config node R2 rtm-route prefix 100.0.0.0/24 4 2 0 2 50 gateway 20.1.1.1 interface eth3


Add L2 ISIS Internal route on R2
:STEP:2
:CMD: config node R2 rtm-route prefix 101.0.0.0/24 4 3 0 2 60 gateway 20.1.1.1 interface eth3


Add L1 ISIS External route on R2
:STEP:3
:CMD: config node R2 rtm-route prefix 102.0.0.0/24 4 4 0 2 70 gateway 20.1.1.1 interface eth3


Add L2 ISIS External route on R2
:STEP:4
:CMD: config node R2 rtm-route prefix 103.0.0.0/24 4 5 0 2 80 gateway 20.1.1.1 interface eth3


Verify all ISIS routes with protocol and metrics
:STEP:5
:CMD: show node R2 ip vrf 0 route 0
:STEP:6
:PATTERN-MATCH:100.0.0.0/24
:STEP:7
:PATTERN-MATCH:ISIS
:STEP:8
:GREP:100.0.0.0/24
:STEP:9
:PATTERN-MATCH:50
:STEP:10
:CMD: show node R2 ip vrf 0 route 0
:STEP:11
:PATTERN-MATCH:101.0.0.0/24
:STEP:12
:GREP:101.0.0.0/24
:STEP:13
:PATTERN-MATCH:60
:STEP:14
:CMD: show node R2 ip vrf 0 route 0
:STEP:15
:PATTERN-MATCH:102.0.0.0/24
:STEP:16
:GREP:102.0.0.0/24
:STEP:17
:PATTERN-MATCH:70
:STEP:18
:CMD: show node R2 ip vrf 0 route 0
:STEP:19
:PATTERN-MATCH:103.0.0.0/24
:STEP:20
:GREP:103.0.0.0/24
:STEP:21
:PATTERN-MATCH:80
:STEP:22
:PATTERN-MATCH:20.1.1.1
:STEP:23
:PATTERN-MATCH:eth3

Delete ISIS routes
:STEP:24
:CMD: config node R2 no rtm-route prefix 100.0.0.0/24 4 2 0 2 50 gateway 20.1.1.1 interface eth3
:STEP:25
:CMD: config node R2 no rtm-route prefix 101.0.0.0/24 4 3 0 2 60 gateway 20.1.1.1 interface eth3
:STEP:26
:CMD: config node R2 no rtm-route prefix 102.0.0.0/24 4 4 0 2 70 gateway 20.1.1.1 interface eth3
:STEP:27
:CMD: config node R2 no rtm-route prefix 103.0.0.0/24 4 5 0 2 80 gateway 20.1.1.1 interface eth3


Verify all ISIS routes are deleted
:STEP:28
:CMD: show node R2 ip vrf 0 route 0
:STEP:29
:PATTERN-NOT-MATCH:100.0.0.0/24
:STEP:30
:PATTERN-NOT-MATCH:101.0.0.0/24
:STEP:31
:PATTERN-NOT-MATCH:102.0.0.0/24
:STEP:32
:PATTERN-NOT-MATCH:103.0.0.0/24

:TESTCASE-END:3


:TESTCASE-BEGIN:4
